// #120, THE 15th KIND OF GATE LIE — the compiler demoted `main` to a trap stub
// and exited 0. `poisoned_fns` replaces a function body with `ud2` when mono
// could not instantiate something it needs; inside a metaprog round that is
// EXPECTED and harmless (the round is superseded, its object thrown away), and
// `mono_scan.cpp`'s own message says so. Surviving into the FINAL emission it
// is neither: MEASURED before the fix — `logosc: wrote …`, rc 0, and the linked
// binary died with SIGILL, rc 132, ZERO destructor calls.
//
// Every pass fixture asserts an exit code, so a compile that replaces `main`
// with a trap and exits 0 is invisible to the corpus BY CONSTRUCTION. Same
// argument that made the `mlir_gen:` channel fatal in #103, one layer up, and
// routed through the SAME sink so it is counted and enforced by one mechanism
// rather than two that could disagree.
//
// ⚠ THE UNDERLYING TYPE DEFECT IS NOT FIXED HERE AND IS NOT THIS FIXTURE'S
// SUBJECT: `and::<i64>` binds the method-level tparam to the wrong slot. What
// this pins is that the compiler REFUSES instead of shipping `ud2`. Its admit
// twin `mono_trap_stub_final_round_ctl` is the same program without the
// turbofish, and it must stay green — a fix that refuses both would be a
// different defect.
package monotrap;
use logos.std.fmt;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let a: Option<i64> = Option::Some(1i64);
    let b: Option<i64> = Option::Some(2i64);
    let c: Option<i64> = a.and::<i64>(b);
    match c { Option::Some(v) => { println!("v={}", v); }, Option::None => { println!("none"); } }
    return 0i32; }
